 "_source": "awk run with sh -c in containers of these images (docker run -d --network none --platform P IMAGE sleep, one docker exec -u 0:0 per case, stdout and stderr apart), 2026-10-22, Docker on linux/arm64 with linux/amd64 under emulation: the cases whose output depends on the platform, recorded on linux/amd64 and linux/arm64. mawk 1.3.4 20250131 (debian:13, amd64; its arm64 cases are in awk_lang.json): rand() without srand, srand() and srand with seeds beyond 32 bits or below 0; BusyBox 1.36.1 (busybox:1.36.1-musl, amd64 and arm64) and 1.25.1 (busybox:1.25, amd64 only): print of 2**63, printf of integer conversions out of the int, srand with a negative or wide seed, CONVFMT=\"%d\", the text a copied number keeps; gawk 5.1.0 (rockylinux:9, amd64 and arm64) and the others: for-in of keys with bytes beyond ASCII. `image` is the index digest, `image_id` the platform image. Volatile (clock-seeded, compared by form): the rand() and srand() cases of mawk on amd64 without a seed and the value srand(5) returns there. Nothing normalised. Locale: LANG and LC_ALL unset (the C locale) in every entry but rockylinux_9_arm64_utf8 (LC_ALL=C.utf8, gawk in its character mode as the persona runs it; the octal escapes beyond ASCII). Recorded 2026-10-27 with `docker run --rm --network none --platform P IMAGE sh -c CASE` on the same images: in the busybox entries the text a copy of a cached number keeps and srand(0); in rockylinux_9_arm64_utf8 the four octal-escape cases (the Invalid multibyte warning of gawk's length() is not emulated).",
